* "American Lead V", channel 3, stage 2 of 2: V1B, CH3 GAIN, V5A, V4B with the feedback R36 / C24 around them and the load R37 / R38, V3A, V6A and CH3 MASTER.
* (V3A's grid conducts at full drive, loading o3a through R39 220k: no cut there.)
* Driven by the main netlist's node go (VGO, V1B's grid). See preamp.net for the assumptions.

V VRAIL x 100 400
* HT supply as on the power supply page (MVSUP): B -> R149 5k6 || R215 4k7 (CH3) -> node C (C87 33u: the plates of V5A, V4B, V3A and V6A) -> R131 1k -> node E (C88 33u: V1A and V1B).
* Each stage here has its own copy and the DC drop kept small, so the resistors are 1k and the capacitors are what makes the corner frequencies of the real filter
* (2k55 x 33u at C = 84u here, 1k x 33u at E = 33u): without that filtering the power amp's sag reached the preamp's first stages at full gain and the channel motorboated.
R R86 x dp 1k
C C87 dp 0 330u
R R131 dp de 1k
C C88 de 0 100u
S VGO go 1 0

* V1B (100k plate, 1k5 with 0.47u), C20 0.047u and the 100k load R35.
T V1B go p1b k1b 12AX7
R R27P de p1b 100k
R R26 k1b 0 1.5k
C C19A k1b 0 0.47u
C C20 p1b v1o 0.047u
R R35 v1o 0 100k

* CH3 GAIN (1MA, wiper pot) behind R51 680k with R52 475k below it; R36 3M3 and C24 20p from V5A / V4B's output back to its input.
R R51 v1o gp 680k
R VRG_T gp wg 1
R VRG_B wg gb 1
R R52 gb 0 475k
C C24 v1o o3a 20p
R R36 v1o o3a 3.3M

* V5A (82k plate, 1k5 with 2u2, 120p grid to cathode) into V4B (0.02u, R55 270k, 1000p and R56 68k at its grid).
T V5A wg p5 k5 12AX7
C C35 wg k5 120p
R R54 dp p5 82k
R R53 k5 0 1.5k
C C36 k5 0 2.2u
C C37 p5 a37 0.02u
R R55 a37 g4 270k
C C38 g4 0 1000p
R R56 g4 0 68k
T V4B g4 p4 k4 12AX7
C C39 g4 k4 120p
R R40 dp p4 270k
R R57 k4 0 3.3k
C C40 k4 c40 0.22u
R SW_BR c40 0 1e12

* V4B's output through C28 0.047u, R39 220k with C27 250p across it, the load R37 680k / R38 100k and the treble shunts C25 47p / C26 500p.
C C28 p4 q 0.047u
R R39 q o3a 220k
C C27 q o3a 250p
R R37 o3a 0 680k
R R38 o3a 0 100k
C C25 o3a 0 47p
C C26 o3a 0 500p

* V3A (shared by the three channels; RYC3C C3 brings channel 3 to its grid): 100k plate, R44 1k5 with C31 100u (J175C) and C32 2u2 (J175B) as cathode bypasses, C33 0.047u.
T V3A o3a p3a k3a 12AX7
R R43 dp p3a 100k
R R44 k3a 0 1.5k
C C31 k3a c31 100u
R SW_C31 c31 0 1e12
C C32 k3a c32 2.2u
R SW_C32 c32 0 1
C C33 p3a u3 0.047u

* To V6A (RYC3E C3): R45 47k, R46 47k to ground, R47 150k and R210 3k3 into the grid; R48 47k to ground, 120p to the cathode, R49 4k7 (mode IV).
R R45 u3 m6 47k
R R46 m6 0 47k
R R47 m6 n6 150k
R R210 n6 g6 3.3k
R R48 g6 0 47k
R SW_R49 g6 r49 1e12
R R49 r49 0 4.7k
T V6A g6 p6 k6 12AX7
C C44 g6 k6 120p
R R62 k6 0 1k
C C104 k6 cx1 4.4u
R SW_M7A cx1 0 1
C C42 k6 cx2 15u
R SW_M7B cx2 0 1e12
R R63 dp p6 120k
C C43 p6 mm 0.047u
R VRMS_T o3 wm 1
R VRMS_B wm 0 1
R WM wm o3 1
R RC43 mm o3 1
